!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/38/orders/orders-1.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/38/io/ltr8/http/meta-service.tn"
!!import:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/38/orders/orders-types-1.tn"
!!import:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/38/orders/orders-errors-1.tn"
@doc:"""
  Interface only: nothing HTTP in the document. An interface is a map of methods keyed by name -- a
  method's name is the key it sits under, scoped to its interface, and a `@doc` before the key documents
  it. The `!method` tag is optional under the typed slot. `extends` names other interfaces whose methods
  this one also has, by references the resolver judges (`orders.orders`: the entry, then its key); the reader
  walks them, not `!!import`. A method stays the interface's that declares it, and a binding names it there.
  """
{
  @doc:"The orders interface."
  orders => !interfaces { orders => {
    @summary:"Place an order."
    @doc:"Accept an order and confirm it with the quantity doubled."
    place_order  => { request: new_order    response: order       errors: [sku_not_found] }
    @safe
    @doc:"One order, by reference."
    get_order    => { request: order_ref    response: order       errors: [order_not_found] }
    @safe
    @doc:"A page of orders, filtered by status."
    list_orders  => { request: order_query  response: order_page }
    @idempotent
    @doc:"Cancel an order. Cancelling twice is the same as cancelling once."
    cancel_order => { request: order_ref    errors: [order_not_found] }
  } }

  @doc:"Everything orders has, and a refund."
  orders_v2 => !interfaces { orders_v2 => {
    extends: [orders.orders]
    methods: {
      @idempotent
      refund => { request: order_ref }
    }
  } }
}
